WEBVTT

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.740
Say, Joe. Mind if I ask you something?

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:16.120
Go ahead.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:21.710
When you got into the ring as Nomad,
why did you have Gear on?

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.590
You probably didn't want people
finding out who you were,

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.840
but I figured it was something else, too.

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:30.300
I've been curious for a while now.

00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:35.430
"Gearless" Joe doesn't belong just to me.

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:39.060
So I donned that Gear as someone else.

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.020
So the opposite of me.

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:46.400
I made my Gear with my son Carlo.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:50.860
You put on that Gear to be alone,

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:54.120
but I put on my Gear
to feel Carlo by my side.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.580
This is basically my good luck charm.

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:03.380
You can't make your mistakes disappear.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:08.090
But if you lose your self-esteem,
you can't live your tomorrow.

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.260
There'll definitely be a day...

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:16.220
...where you get back into that ring.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:25.520
We didn't find any major injuries
such as blood clots or an aneurysm...

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:31.610
...but he must have been suffering from
headaches from quite some time now.

00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:35.820
There were signs of inflammation and
ulcerations in his digestive system,

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:40.160
so he was probably addicted
to shoddy painkillers for years.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:44.500
We're talking about before
he came back here.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.170
He's told me about this.

00:01:46.170 --> 00:01:50.050
But now he's stopped using them and
said he wasn't having headaches anymore.

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.880
There isn't a single boxer in this world
that doesn't have some brain damage.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:02:00.100
It's not rare that they feel aftereffects
from cerebral hemorrhages or contusions.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:02.810
Some cases may even lead to death.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.980
MEGALOBOX 2

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:21.790
Where's Sachio? Did he leave?

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:25.830
Yeah. He went to get his
things from Drunk Monk.

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:30.460
Look. He's not so pale anymore
and his tests came back fine.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:36.760
How can he be fine?
He suddenly passed out.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:40.390
Is your head okay?
Do you feel nauseous at all?

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:42.310
I'm fine now.

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:44.180
Sorry for making you guys worry.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.690
Pops said the same thing at first. But--

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:48.900
Don't even say stuff like that!

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.690
Especially when he's got his
match with Mac coming up.

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:55.280
But you said it might be
punch-drunk syndrome!

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.030
I was freaked out, too, okay?!

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:07.540
To be honest, I was shocked to hear
that you were addicted to painkillers.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:17.340
Promise us that you won't lie or
hide anything from us anymore.

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:20.890
I will. I won't betray
you guys ever again.

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:25.390
The repairs to the gym will be done soon.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:27.440
When they are, I want
all of you to come by.

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.770
Perfect timing.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:32.320
We can throw a party celebrating
that and your recovery!

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:34.940
I'll make tons of good food.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.570
Yeah, that sounds great!

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:54.800
You're from Shirato...

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.720
Side effects from the brain chip?

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:09.850
This thesis is still hypothetical, but if
there is even the slightest chance

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:13.650
that Mac's health might be affected,

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:16.240
Shirato would be partially responsible

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.780
since we are involved
in manufacturing BES.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:22.320
But why are you telling me this?

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:26.620
We figured you might know something
because you're his family.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:30.040
You might've noticed minor changes
to him that he hasn't realized himself.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.460
I haven't really noticed anything...

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:38.260
He's been relaxing after his fights
and getting plenty of sleep.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:41.720
Here!

00:04:42.930 --> 00:04:44.350
Why, thank you.

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:45.560
Ah...

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:55.270
I'm glad things worked out.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:05:00.450
Well, I'd heard about Miguel's
transplant surgery.

00:05:00.450 --> 00:05:02.820
You had miraculously
managed to find a donor.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.170
The goal behind this foundation
that we had just established

00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:19.420
is to build hospitals in the areas
where the military has withdrawn.

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:22.680
Enhancements in medicine not only
leads to more infrastructure,

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:27.680
but will immediately aid the
people in the affected areas...

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:34.350
I believe that their son's surgery took
place right around the time Mac

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:37.570
agreed to be a part of
BES's treatment program.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:38.480
Yes.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:42.070
She didn't seem to want to talk about it
and immediately changed the subject.

00:05:43.860 --> 00:05:46.030
I'm sure it was a very hard time for them,

00:05:46.030 --> 00:05:48.120
so that's hardly surprising.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:06:00.090
Impressive, President Shirato.
What a fancy surprise.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:08.810
Surprise! I totally came here uninvited!

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:10.680
Yukiko! Please, come back to the stage!

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:15.350
Allow you me to congratulate
you personally, Yukiko!

00:06:15.350 --> 00:06:18.400
How nice of you to make time out
of your busy schedule to come by.

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.690
You're just full of surprises.

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:26.620
But of course! We are partners
in our valiant efforts.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:30.490
Though, sadly, that partnership
doesn't extend into our private lives.

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:35.120
I'm sure you were quite surprised
to hear about the match with Joe.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:37.250
I mean, I didn't even discuss it with you.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:42.210
No, as I'm sure there's something
behind that surprise.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:48.180
I was quite surprised myself when
you started using spy tactics!

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.350
Now, everyone.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:54.520
Let us make a toast to a
future brimming with hope!

00:06:55.390 --> 00:07:04.400
"Team Nowhere"

00:07:01.900 --> 00:07:04.320
Come on, Santa. Help.

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.320
Hey! There won't be enough!

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:10.120
Jeez...

00:07:10.120 --> 00:07:11.200
It's so pretty.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:15.410
Before I came back here,
I was in a town called Casa.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:18.500
Once a year, they have a festival where
they decorate the place with flowers

00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:21.420
and welcome back their
family that's passed on.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:23.960
So you did this for Pops?

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.090
Yeah.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:27.130
I'm sure he loves it.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:29.220
He's probably right around the corner.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:36.690
Thank you all for gathering here today...

00:07:36.690 --> 00:07:39.270
Pops was so nervous.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:41.230
He was practicing in secret.

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:47.360
I overhauled your ride for you.

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:52.660
Boss worked on it while
you were in the hospital.

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:54.910
It needed work all over.

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:59.420
It's been bugging me ever
since you came back.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:02.420
I never thought I'd get you
to fix 'er up ever again.

00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:06.340
Well, you didn't give up fixing
up this place, so you win.

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:09.890
I figured I could believe in you again.

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:10.970
Thanks.

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:13.060
Sure.

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:15.020
What's Sachio doing?

00:08:16.020 --> 00:08:19.060
Who knows? By the way, Joe.

00:08:19.060 --> 00:08:21.690
Now's the perfect time to tell
us what you've been through.

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:23.190
Come on, Santa!

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:25.610
Well, of course I'm gonna ask him that!

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.650
I'm a freelance journalist, after all!

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:28.530
But...

00:08:28.530 --> 00:08:30.530
It's fine.

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:34.030
That's another reason I
gathered you all here today.

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:43.460
Once I left this place, I got back
into the ring underground.

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:50.880
I drifted from one town to the next
and eventually lost track of all time.

00:08:50.880 --> 00:08:54.390
I told myself over and over that
I'd go home the next day.

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:56.350
But in the end,

00:08:56.350 --> 00:09:01.060
I just kept getting back into the ring,
letting the painkillers numb the pain.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:05.400
Just like when I got into the ring
with Liu, saying it was for Pops.

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:11.200
And that's when I met this guy...

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:27.250
So Chief died then?

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:33.140
Yeah... But Chief's legacy lives
on with everyone in Casa.

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:34.760
And it will forever.

00:09:38.060 --> 00:09:42.640
The reason I was able to get off
those drugs and come back here

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:44.560
is all thanks to Chief.

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:47.650
I wanted to tell you all that.

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:58.080
Yuri...

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:07.620
"Team Nowhere"

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:07.540
Five years ago...

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:12.510
Pops just wanted to live out the
last moments of his life in peace

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:14.220
and I took that from him.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:20.680
I agreed to that match without
talking to any of you first.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:22.600
Of course, I was gonna lose.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:30.780
Just because I'm off the drugs now doesn't
mean my body's back in its prime.

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:33.450
Who knows what's gonna happen
if I get back in that ring again?

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:39.370
All I know is that the next match
is gonna be my final one.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:42.870
That's why I want all of
you to help me decide

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:45.370
if I should do this match or not.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:49.670
If I should fight one last time
as part of Team Nowhere.

00:10:51.130 --> 00:10:52.970
I don't want you to fight.

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:57.090
What the hell, man?! You were
happier than anyone about this!

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.350
But I don't want Joe to die.

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:02.020
I don't want to lose any more family!

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:03.980
Yeah, but...

00:11:03.980 --> 00:11:06.810
I'm fine with either option.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:10.070
I feel the same as Bonjiri,

00:11:10.070 --> 00:11:13.360
but now, Joe's come clean with us.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:16.820
That's why I'll respect
Joe's decision with this.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:25.750
I still haven't forgiven you.

00:11:25.750 --> 00:11:27.880
I probably never will.

00:11:29.670 --> 00:11:33.550
But when I got into the ring
with you the other day,

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:35.630
I figured I could maybe
get past this whole

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:39.220
forgiving your not forgiving you thing.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:44.850
I'm gonna live my own life to the fullest.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:49.650
You want to fight Mac, don't you?

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:51.650
Yeah.

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:56.110
If shit goes down, I don't care what
anyone says. I'm throwing in the towel.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:57.740
Those are my terms.

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:03.580
Guess we need to get back to training.

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:13.630
Yuri...

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:17.510
Liu asked me to stay by your side.

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:26.060
Man, I've been waiting for this moment!

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:28.310
"Gearless" Joe is finally back, baby!

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:30.690
Sorry, Santa.

00:12:30.690 --> 00:12:32.230
That's not exactly true.

00:12:39.910 --> 00:12:45.830
In my last fight, I want to just
be me and fight with this.

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:50.080
This is Chief's keepsake.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:54.960
It's a special Gear that his son
Carlo customized just for his dad.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:59.090
Chief always fought
with Carlo by his side.

00:12:59.090 --> 00:13:03.430
This always protected him so that
he could come back home safe.

00:13:03.430 --> 00:13:05.260
So I...

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:07.770
...also want to put this gear on

00:13:07.770 --> 00:13:09.730
so I can live the rest of
my life with all of you.

00:13:23.240 --> 00:13:28.290
I've wanted to fix up this
place for a long time.

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:30.500
I know.

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:35.340
I'm sure Pops would have no problem
coming back here with all these flowers.

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:36.590
Yeah.

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:40.960
"Team Nowhere"

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.690
The match is finally official.

00:13:52.690 --> 00:13:53.400
Yes.

00:13:53.470 --> 00:13:56.350
"Feature - The Exhibition Match Between the Hero and the Legend Becomes a Reality!!"

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:55.610
But it's hard to say that

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:59.400
they're on the same level.

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:02.070
Everyone's got their eyes on Joe as the

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:05.030
legendary boxer officially
makes his return to the ring.

00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:09.620
But Mac managed to defeat
the eternal champion, Liu.

00:14:09.620 --> 00:14:12.540
He is truly one of the best.

00:14:26.050 --> 00:14:30.770
His readings are reaching dangerous
levels even sooner now.

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:33.850
And?

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:35.730
Huh? Er...

00:14:35.730 --> 00:14:39.780
What I'm trying to say is even
if his physical abilities increase,

00:14:39.780 --> 00:14:42.690
that's causing quite a
burden on his brain.

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:45.240
At this rate, Mac's body won't hold up.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:50.040
The price of high-spec integration.

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:54.120
We just need to concentrate
on him performing his best.

00:14:55.170 --> 00:14:59.750
Just adjust the numbers
to the usual levels.

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:00.500
But--

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:04.090
It's that hesitation that's going
to close the doors to the future.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:08.720
Don't you agree?

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:09.930
Yes.

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.170
Did I do this?

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:41.090
This isn't the first time.

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:43.130
You've done this countless times.

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:48.590
Please, don't do any more matches.

00:15:49.970 --> 00:15:53.600
I'll make this up to you.
But this match is...

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:54.810
Read this!

00:15:56.270 --> 00:16:00.810
What you just did matches
the symptoms listed in there.

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:03.610
Those are nothing but lies.

00:16:03.610 --> 00:16:07.320
If there was actually something wrong,
Mr. Sakuma would've told me!

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.290
There's nothing to worry about.

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:17.920
I want you to believe
in me and Mr. Sakuma.

00:16:19.580 --> 00:16:22.420
You're not yourself anymore.

00:16:23.590 --> 00:16:25.380
Maya...

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:28.220
I'm the one who did this to you!

00:16:29.930 --> 00:16:31.970
Wait.

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:34.930
What are you talking about, Maya?

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:36.310
Get away!

00:16:51.320 --> 00:16:56.120
That day... The day you were
involved in that shootout...

00:16:56.120 --> 00:16:58.160
Sakuma appeared at the hospital

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:01.460
and proposed the BES treatment program.

00:17:01.460 --> 00:17:08.170
Miguel was sick, and I didn't
know when you'd wake up...

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:10.090
You made the right choice.

00:17:10.090 --> 00:17:11.760
You and ROSCO saved me

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:14.350
from being bedridden the
rest of my life, didn't you?

00:17:15.890 --> 00:17:19.520
There was a chance you
were going to recover.

00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:24.570
You might've been able to walk again
with extensive physical therapy...

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:27.860
But you ended up with a body
that'll never be able to move on

00:17:27.860 --> 00:17:30.610
its own again because of
the BES treatment program!

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:34.160
But that's... Why would you...?

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:37.120
Sakuma had prepared a donor for us.

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:43.330
I ended up signing the contract
in exchange for Miguel's surgery.

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:51.300
You did this to my body
all for some experiment?

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:56.260
I might've lost both you and Miguel.

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:57.470
I just...

00:17:59.770 --> 00:18:03.980
You're currently in the exact
position Joe was in back then.

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:06.980
Come on. Let's dream together again.

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:26.090
Ah, that. That's just nonsense
from a wannabe researcher.

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:27.290
We're officially asking for that to be--

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:30.800
Everything in here is true.

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:34.550
I knew that something was wrong with me,

00:18:34.550 --> 00:18:37.600
but I just continued to lie to my family.

00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:41.270
But Maya's never lied to me before.

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:46.230
She told me everything earlier.

00:18:46.230 --> 00:18:48.110
Including what happened with Miguel.

00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:51.030
And the fact that you just
used me as a guinea pig.

00:18:55.780 --> 00:19:00.620
I figured Maya would tell you even sooner.

00:19:01.790 --> 00:19:04.040
I mean, you're husband and wife.

00:19:04.040 --> 00:19:06.710
Isn't it hard keeping
secrets from each other?

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:14.010
So I'd always thought it was possible
you already knew the truth.

00:19:14.010 --> 00:19:17.390
That you understood that this
was for the greater good.

00:19:17.390 --> 00:19:20.850
But... I guess that's too good to be true.

00:19:21.890 --> 00:19:24.310
Do people's lives mean nothing to you?

00:19:24.310 --> 00:19:27.860
I was certain that BES would work.

00:19:27.860 --> 00:19:31.440
And because of that, you're now at
the top of the Megalo-boxing world,

00:19:31.440 --> 00:19:34.070
and a hero.

00:19:34.070 --> 00:19:38.620
You've achieved something your
former self never could've reached.

00:19:38.620 --> 00:19:40.830
Isn't that right? Can you
actually say I'm wrong?

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:44.790
Hero my ass. It's all a bunch
of lies you made up!

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:48.130
That's not true.

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:49.710
You created this.

00:19:51.090 --> 00:19:55.050
I never anticipated Mac Time.

00:19:55.050 --> 00:19:56.930
That's a miracle you created.

00:19:56.930 --> 00:20:00.050
Drop the bullshit! That's no miracle!

00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:03.310
Then what about Miguel?

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:08.190
The reason he was cured was because
you went through this program.

00:20:08.190 --> 00:20:12.190
You said it yourself.
He's a miracle child.

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:16.030
Maya just opted for a future
brimming with hope.

00:20:21.030 --> 00:20:26.910
Once BES gets put out on the market,
it's going to save countless lives.

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:29.960
That future is right around the corner.

00:20:33.050 --> 00:20:34.550
You're not just some onlooker

00:20:34.550 --> 00:20:36.840
looking up at a legend anymore.

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:40.340
You're a true hero.

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:51.440
Sizzle, sizzle.

00:20:51.440 --> 00:20:56.110
Around the time the harsh sun rose up
into the sky and shone upon the land,

00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:58.400
the hummingbird appeared
before the nomad again,

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:01.620
who was exhausted from walking.

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:06.750
"Nomad, please listen to
my song one more time."

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:08.620
Keep moving!

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:11.170
No matter how hard the nomad
tried to shoo the bird away,

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:13.960
it refused to leave his side.

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:23.510
"If I can get you to lie again, will you
listen to my song once more?"

00:21:23.510 --> 00:21:28.560
"I already told you.
I'm on this journey to die.

00:21:28.560 --> 00:21:32.020
I have no reason to lie anymore."

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:36.650
The frustrated nomad was
sure he could win this time

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:39.650
and agreed to the hummingbird's terms.

00:21:36.650 --> 00:21:39.650
You should come by my place sometime.

00:21:39.650 --> 00:21:43.200
"Why do you want to die?"

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:49.160
"I may have the eyes to see you,
ears to hear your song,

00:21:49.160 --> 00:21:56.300
and a mouth to speak to you,
but I've lost everything else."

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:52.370
"ROSCO Saves Injured Police Officer!!"

00:21:56.300 --> 00:21:58.960
And then, the Hummingbird replied,

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:03.800
"No. You also have the
hands to shoo me away

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:08.060
and legs to take you on this journey."

00:22:08.060 --> 00:22:12.810
"Yes, you are right. You win again."

00:22:14.610 --> 00:22:20.190
And so, the nomad listened to the
hummingbird's song once more.

00:22:20.190 --> 00:22:24.490
This song was even more
beautiful than the last

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:27.200
and the nomad felt solace in his heart.

00:22:28.910 --> 00:22:32.830
The hummingbird seemed
satisfied as it finished its song

00:22:32.830 --> 00:22:36.590
and then flew off into the wind.
